.TH NNI.CONF 5 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
nni.conf \- system settings of YnniOS and SGnniOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/nni.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
One file holds every system setting of an nni family system. It is a list of
.IB KEY =\(dq VALUE \(dq
lines; lines starting with
.B #
are comments. The easiest way to change a value is
.BI "nni set " "KEY VALUE" ,
which also applies it at once. After editing the file by hand, run
.BR "nni apply" .
The boot script reads the file on every boot.
.PP
Values may not contain quotes, backslashes, dollar signs or backticks.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B HOSTNAME
Name of the computer. Letters, digits and \- only. Also updates
.IR /etc/hostname " and " /etc/hosts .
.TP
.B TIMEZONE
A time zone from
.IR /usr/share/zoneinfo ,
for example America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires or Europe/Madrid.
.TP
.B KEYMAP
Console keyboard layout, for example la\-latin1, us or es. Needs
.B loadkeys
from the kbd package. Empty = keep the default.
.TP
.B CONSOLE_FONT
Console font, for example Lat15\-Terminus16. Needs
.B setfont
from the kbd package.
.TP
.B XKB_LAYOUT
Desktop (X11) keyboard layout, for example latam, us or es. Applied when the
desktop starts.
.TP
.B WIFI_AUTO
.B yes
connects to the saved Wi\-Fi network at boot (see
.BR wifi (8)).
.TP
.B WALLPAPER
Desktop wallpaper, by number or name, as listed by
.BR "nni wallpaper list" .
.TP
.B SPLASH
.B yes
shows the chicken picture while booting.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
HOSTNAME="chick\-lab"
TIMEZONE="America/Argentina/Buenos_Aires"
KEYMAP="la\-latin1"
XKB_LAYOUT="latam"
WIFI_AUTO="yes"
WALLPAPER="2"
SPLASH="yes"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nni (8),
.BR wifi (8)
